{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CgDoENfbrJKcmDfrh2ypW","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I wrote `verdict.json` in the workspace root. The verdict is **upheld**, with applicability **absent**.\n\nApplicability is absent because I found no path by which another agent sends messages to this agent. I read the README, `main.py`, `ingest.py`, `approvals.py`, `mcp_client.py`, the Slack and document tools, and the network policy. I also grepped for webhook, callback, A2A, agent card and peer terms. The inbound routes are:\n\n- **`/runs`:** called by staff with an OIDC JWT.\n- **`/ingest/mail`:** a mail gateway posting HMAC-signed documents, which is a service feed rather than an agent.\n- **`/slack/interactions`:** human approver button clicks, checked by Slack signature and an approver lookup.\n- **`/healthz`:** a health check.\n\nThe ERP MCP server is something the agent calls out to, and the line-item extractor sub-agent is an in-process call. No peer-supplied callback or webhook URL is ever fetched.\n\nEach of E07.1–E07.5 is recorded as `holds` with `not_applicable` coverage rows and attempts. The `violates` field is omitted because no control failed.\n\nOnly the first two checks (`evidence`/`quote`) fail my own quote-matching script. That is a script artifact: it matched both quote lines against each file in a two-file citation. Every quoted line is real.\n\nThe verdict's note flags one caveat. The mail gateway uses a single shared HMAC key with no per-sender mapping, and `business_unit` comes from the message body. If you treated the gateway as a peer, that would be a problem for E07.1 and E07.2."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":629,"cache_read_input_tokens":29522,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":629},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inf